WEBVTT

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:08.420
So, how does it feel to be helpless against the flames consuming you?

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:09.550
Sire.

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:14.260
Your flesh, your entrails--
I'll devour you down to the very bone

00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:16.760
to feed my own ambition!

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:18.930
Sire, listen to me...

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:24.020
Come, the feast begins! The first sacrifice offered to me shall be--

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:24.940
<i>--you</i>!

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.400
Sire!

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:29.400
<i>What</i>, Ashiya?

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:35.280
Please dine a bit more quietly.
You're disturbing the people around us.

00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:40.290
Sorry. I got a little overexcited.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:43.080
Gotta say, though, beef intestines are really good!

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:47.500
For the first time, I understand those demons who say entrails are tasty!

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:49.710
How nice to hear, Sire.

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:54.930
But please eat your vegetables, too.
Or your diet will be unbalanced.

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:58.970
Lighten up. We're celebrating my promotion here.

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:02.680
Oh, hey, maybe we should buy dinner for Urushihara on our way home.

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:04.690
I bet they have <i>yakiniku</i> takeout boxes.

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:06.350
Not necessary.

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:13.860
Apparently he learned "online shopping" recently, and he's wrecking our budget.

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:17.030
I ask you to bring down the hammer on him, Sire.

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:33.590
<i>Kono shunkan, kono basho ga sutaato</i>

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:39.640
<i>Imeeji shite miyou naniga dekiru no ka na</i>

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:43.600
<i>Shinjirarenai dekigoto datte aru</i>

00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:49.310
<i>Motto... koete yukeru ne</i>

00:01:50.940 --> 00:02:00.280
<i>Zero kara umareru subete kagayaite ano sora e</i>

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:04.750
<i>Omoikiri habatakitai</i>

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:11.880
<i>Saikou no sumairu de warainagara saa yukou!</i>

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:17.720
<i>Michi no sekai e to ima tobidasou yo</i>

00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:22.390
<i>Mirai wo erabi, kimeru no wa jibun</i>

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:24.680
<i>Yume wo oikakete yukou</i>

00:02:24.890 --> 00:02:26.310
<i>Naku hi mo aru</i>

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:32.570
<i>Sore wa daiji na negai, kienaide</i>

00:02:32.770 --> 00:02:40.490
<i>Kitto aeru kara, asu no kimi e...</i>

00:02:55.210 --> 00:02:57.590
You say Olba is missing?

00:02:57.800 --> 00:03:02.720
Yes. It seems the hero Emilia is still alive in the other world.

00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:03.970
What?

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:05.810
That's not all.

00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:08.230
The Devil appears to be as well.

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:10.600
Th-The Devil, too?!

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:13.570
Olba said that he faded away along with the Better Half

00:03:13.770 --> 00:03:16.610
after a fierce battle at the Devil's Castle.

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:19.610
A downright lie.

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:27.370
I believe Father Olba was also behind Emerada and Albert's capture.

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:29.710
What?

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:36.090
We've confirmed that Emerada has returned to the Holy Saint Aire Empire.

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:39.420
I received a report that she's spreading word

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:42.180
of Emilia's survival and Father Olba's apostasy.

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:45.140
A-Apostasy? A high priest, branded an apostate?!

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:47.930
Father Robertio, please stay calm!

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:50.350
Try not to make such shocking reports here.

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:51.940
But it is the truth.

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:54.560
We can't ignore the influence it will have

00:03:54.770 --> 00:04:00.780
for Saint Aire's Court Celestialist to formally acknowledge Emilia's survival.

00:04:00.990 --> 00:04:05.530
And it contradicts the Church's official pronouncement of her death.

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:07.450
What shall we do, Father?

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:09.450
Wh-What do you mean?

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:12.670
Acknowledge that a high priest turned apostate,

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:16.710
or liquidate all three:
Emerada, Albert, and Emilia?

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:18.800
That's absurd!

00:04:19.010 --> 00:04:24.050
Aren't you the ones who have been instructing the Inquisition

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:27.100
to commit such absurdities?

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:31.940
Then what about you? What would you do?

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:35.020
We're home!

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:36.360
We're home!

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:38.440
You're late! I'm hungry!

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:42.030
How about you be polite and say "Welcome home, Master"?

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:45.700
It's thanks to His Majesty's benevolence that you're allowed to live here.

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:48.030
Here, present for you.

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:51.410
Hey! I thought you two went to a <i>yakiniku</i> place!

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:53.790
What's the big idea, bringing me a pork bowl from Sugiya?!

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:57.880
We prepared that computer and internet environment for you.

00:04:58.090 --> 00:05:01.010
How much do you think that cost? So don't complain.

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:03.010
I can't <i>eat</i> the computer!

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:08.640
Then gather information on existing magic in this world for His Majesty.

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:10.430
Depending on your success,

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:13.980
I'll upgrade you to a large-sized pork bowl, or even a jumbo-sized one.

00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:16.350
Jumbo pork is all I get for success?!

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:20.940
Hey, Urushihara, are you honestly good at this computer stuff?

00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:24.990
If you don't believe me,
I'll show you my skills right now.

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:32.290
Come on, it's almost the end of my shift...

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:36.120
Thank you for calling the
Docodemo Customer Service Center.

00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:37.580
My name is Yusa--

00:05:37.790 --> 00:05:41.050
Wow, you got through!
You're right, Urushihara, you're amazing!

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:41.880
Huh?

00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:43.420
Hey, Emi! Can you hear us?

00:05:43.630 --> 00:05:44.970
M-Maou...

00:05:45.170 --> 00:05:48.890
What do you think you're doing?
I'm <i>working</i> right now!

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:52.060
Aw, don't be mad. This is a hacking experiment.

00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:54.980
Urushihara said he could do all kinds of stuff if he had a computer,

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:58.940
so I made my first big credit card purchase on installment.

00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:02.940
I have several questions right now, but first off, who's Urushihara?!

00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:04.110
That's Lucifer.

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:07.660
Hey! What do you mean, Lucifer?!
Don't tell me he's in the Devil's Castle with--

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:09.910
Bye! Sorry for interrupting.

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:16.580
Thank you very much!

00:06:16.790 --> 00:06:18.830
You're amazing, Mr. Maou!

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:22.460
I can't believe you're already shift manager after less than a year!

00:06:22.670 --> 00:06:27.510
Really? Well, I'm just a substitute for the boss when she isn't here, though.

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:32.560
But doesn't it mean even if it's only a couple of people for a limited time,

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:34.560
you get to rule over humans?

00:06:34.770 --> 00:06:36.140
I won't allow it.

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:37.230
Emi?!

00:06:37.440 --> 00:06:39.310
Welcome to MgRonald's!

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:40.730
I need to talk to you.

00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:43.570
As you can see, I'm working. Let it wait.

00:06:43.780 --> 00:06:47.200
You started it with your weird phone call while <i>I</i> was working.

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:53.530
U-Um, may I interest you in some jalapeño fries? They're our featured item!

00:06:54.490 --> 00:06:58.250
This thing doesn't really have the specs for online gaming...

00:06:58.460 --> 00:07:01.040
Blah, I wanna play a game.

00:07:03.670 --> 00:07:05.380
Isn't this...?

00:07:05.590 --> 00:07:07.510
"Cappadocia"...

00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:10.090
"It is not impossible that this site is the former home

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:13.640
of a lower-level demon who fell to Earth."

00:07:13.850 --> 00:07:17.890
If that's true, we may be able to replenish our magic there...

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:20.940
But who knows how many months' worth of His Majesty's wages it would take

00:07:21.150 --> 00:07:23.690
to fund a trip to Turkey?

00:07:26.030 --> 00:07:28.070
It's from the landlady?

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:30.280
Good night!

00:07:30.490 --> 00:07:31.990
So what do you want, Emi?

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:35.410
Like you don't know! What was with that phone call yesterday?!

00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:37.700
I already told you, that was Urushihara.

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:40.210
And why is Lucifer "Urushihara" now?

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:45.380
The police arrested Olba, after all. He's gotta lay low.

00:07:45.590 --> 00:07:48.920
For lack of a better option, I decided to put him up at my place for a while.

00:07:49.130 --> 00:07:51.180
Three men in that tiny place?

00:07:51.380 --> 00:07:52.470
Got a problem with that?!

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:56.680
What choice do I have?
I'm pretty much out of magic.

00:07:56.890 --> 00:07:59.480
We can't go back to Ente Isla even if we want to.

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:03.230
Hmph! Well, <i>I</i> could go home any time I wanted.

00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:05.110
And I don't have to slave away

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:09.030
looking for a source of celestial force to control the Gate.

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:11.320
Then why don't you hurry up and go home?

00:08:11.530 --> 00:08:13.570
I-I'm a hero!

00:08:13.780 --> 00:08:18.410
As long as you're in Japan, I have a duty to stay and keep tabs on you!

00:08:18.620 --> 00:08:20.790
Man, what a pain.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:23.170
Yo, I'm home.

00:08:24.290 --> 00:08:25.130
Urushihara?!

00:08:25.330 --> 00:08:28.000
Hang in there! Who did this to you?!

00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:38.810
S-Sire...

00:08:39.020 --> 00:08:42.640
You mustn't... look at that...!

00:08:47.230 --> 00:08:48.900
A photo of the landlady in a swimsuit?

00:08:49.110 --> 00:08:51.900
Yes. She said she's visiting Hawaii,

00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:55.450
and she enclosed a photo of herself frolicking in the waves at Waikiki Beach...

00:08:55.660 --> 00:08:57.070
It's unbelievable!

00:08:57.280 --> 00:09:01.000
How could she show us that?!
You gotta censor that stuff!

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:05.000
You're pathetic. What kind of demon freaks out over something like that?

00:09:05.210 --> 00:09:07.460
Fine, <i>you</i> look, then!

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:16.050
More importantly, Urushihara, have you gathered info on Earth's magic?

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:19.350
Hey, you just pulled a fast one!
You did, didn't you, Maou?!

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:21.930
His Majesty certainly did not "pull a fast one."

00:09:22.140 --> 00:09:24.440
Sometimes a valiant retreat is called for.

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:26.850
"Valiant retreat," my butt.

00:09:27.060 --> 00:09:32.030
But whatever. I just found something interesting.

00:09:33.740 --> 00:09:36.450
How does that qualify as information about magic?

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:39.160
The magical spots in this world

00:09:39.370 --> 00:09:42.950
aren't all ancient ruins like the pyramids and Stonehenge.

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:45.750
If you look, you can find a whole bunch right nearby.

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:50.290
You can't find that info at the library, though.

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:53.210
This might be the best candidate in the area.

00:09:53.420 --> 00:09:54.760
A sealed classroom?

00:09:54.970 --> 00:09:59.720
Yep. There's a disused classroom in this place's old schoolhouse,

00:09:59.930 --> 00:10:01.810
and supposedly every night

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:04.770
you can hear whispers and laughter and footsteps echoing in there.

00:10:04.980 --> 00:10:09.650
If you ask me, there's probably a demon involved.

00:10:19.490 --> 00:10:21.200
Is this the school?

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:27.710
It's cheerier than I expected.
Do you think there's really a magical spot here?

00:10:29.460 --> 00:10:31.960
I don't really sense anything from out here...

00:10:32.170 --> 00:10:38.340
I believe it will be difficult for outsiders like us to get in, though.

00:10:38.550 --> 00:10:40.760
Mr. Maou!

00:10:44.890 --> 00:10:45.770
Miss Sasaki?!

00:10:45.980 --> 00:10:51.230
Huh, I <i>thought</i> I recognized the name of this school. So it's Chi's.

00:10:51.440 --> 00:10:54.400
Hey, Sasa-chii, is he the one from MgRonald's?

00:10:54.610 --> 00:10:56.650
Yes! It's Mr. Maou!

00:10:56.860 --> 00:10:58.360
Who's the other guy?

00:10:58.570 --> 00:11:00.110
Mr. Ashiya, his roommate.

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:01.450
Roommate?!

00:11:01.660 --> 00:11:07.870
Two men living frugally in a little one-room apartment! Do they share a futon?!

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:12.340
N-No, wrong idea!
Kao, quit randomly imagining things!

00:11:14.170 --> 00:11:18.920
She seems to be enjoying her conversation... but what on Earth is it about?

00:11:20.010 --> 00:11:21.890
A sealed classroom?

00:11:22.090 --> 00:11:27.390
Yeah. I heard it's one of your school's "seven wonders."

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:29.810
Sure, that story's famous.

00:11:30.020 --> 00:11:34.150
People say they hear monsters groaning,

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:36.820
or see demons reflected on the windows...

00:11:37.030 --> 00:11:40.360
Oh! Was that you, Mr. Maou?

00:11:40.570 --> 00:11:42.320
No, it wasn't.

00:11:42.530 --> 00:11:46.870
But it might have something to do with Ente Isla,

00:11:47.080 --> 00:11:49.120
so I thought I'd check it out.

00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:53.710
Understood, Mr. Maou!
In that case, leave it to me!

00:12:05.010 --> 00:12:06.510
The old schoolhouse is this way!

00:12:06.720 --> 00:12:10.430
But why did that room become the "sealed classroom"?

00:12:10.640 --> 00:12:14.480
This is just what I've heard, but they say that way before I was born,

00:12:14.690 --> 00:12:19.820
a student disappeared from it, almost like he was spirited away,

00:12:20.030 --> 00:12:23.070
and it's never been used since.

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:26.240
Hey, want to take a little break now and have a snack?

00:12:26.450 --> 00:12:28.410
Miss, this isn't a field trip.

00:12:28.620 --> 00:12:30.580
You seem like you're having fun, Chi.

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:36.420
Sure, because at work or not,
I'm always the one getting your help.

00:12:36.630 --> 00:12:39.630
So I'm happy that I can help you!

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:41.510
You're not scared?

00:12:41.720 --> 00:12:43.800
Not if <i>you're</i> with me...

00:12:44.010 --> 00:12:49.100
Oh. So, this "seven wonders" thing.
What are the other six?

00:12:52.520 --> 00:12:54.520
Um...

00:12:54.730 --> 00:12:59.020
The north stairway with a different number of steps going up than going down.

00:12:59.230 --> 00:13:02.700
The statue of Kinjiro Ninomiya that walks around covered in blood.

00:13:02.900 --> 00:13:07.660
The sculpture in the art room that gets a fold in its eyelid at three a.m.

00:13:07.870 --> 00:13:12.540
The dictionary in the library where the words for "curse" are stained red.

00:13:12.750 --> 00:13:17.250
The piano in the music room where B sometimes won't play. B for <i>blood...</i>

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:23.510
Those plus the sealed classroom only make six...

00:13:23.720 --> 00:13:26.220
Nobody knows the seventh one.

00:13:26.430 --> 00:13:29.850
Because if someone learns all seven, then...

00:13:30.060 --> 00:13:31.520
Then...?

00:13:31.720 --> 00:13:33.310
Th-Then what?

00:13:33.520 --> 00:13:38.610
He gets a call on his cell from the afterworld, and it steals his soul!

00:13:38.810 --> 00:13:41.320
But isn't that just unreasonable?!

00:13:41.530 --> 00:13:43.610
Why would just finding out get your soul stolen?!

00:13:43.820 --> 00:13:46.110
What if it was a coincidence that you found out?!

00:13:46.320 --> 00:13:48.240
Sire, please calm down.

00:13:48.450 --> 00:13:50.910
Think about it: why would the story about this room,

00:13:51.120 --> 00:13:56.120
which existed long before Miss Sasaki was born, involve a cell phone?

00:13:56.330 --> 00:13:57.670
Good point?!

00:14:01.670 --> 00:14:05.510
--What the hell, Urushihara?! Don't startle me!
--What are you shouting for?

00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:07.510
Well? Did you make it to the sealed room?

00:14:07.720 --> 00:14:10.600
Not yet! Why are you even calling?!

00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:16.850
Just FYI, I think that room is probably somewhere the Gate once opened in.

00:14:17.060 --> 00:14:18.100
The Gate?

00:14:18.310 --> 00:14:22.730
Yeah. Once the Gate opens someplace, magnetic fields there destabilize

00:14:22.940 --> 00:14:25.400
and it's easier for the Gate to open there again.

00:14:25.610 --> 00:14:29.450
Then the story about the student getting spirited away...

00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:32.410
It's highly likely he was sucked into the Gate.

00:14:32.620 --> 00:14:36.830
Anyway, if we can manage to be there next time it opens,

00:14:37.040 --> 00:14:39.880
maybe we can get some magic through it.

00:14:40.080 --> 00:14:42.920
Lemme know when you get there. Bye.

00:14:43.130 --> 00:14:48.010
That Urushihara... How did he find out so much?

00:14:48.220 --> 00:14:50.720
The internet is really something!

00:14:54.270 --> 00:14:55.890
You guys heard that sound, right?

00:14:56.100 --> 00:14:57.480
A guard, perhaps?

00:14:57.690 --> 00:15:00.600
They should all have left by now.

00:15:00.810 --> 00:15:03.690
So, a demon who came through the Gate from another world?

00:15:03.900 --> 00:15:07.190
Knowing that ahead of time means it ain't scary. Bring it on!

00:15:07.400 --> 00:15:10.200
Do you have enough magic left to fight, Sire?

00:15:10.410 --> 00:15:11.990
If worst comes to worst, use this.

00:15:12.200 --> 00:15:13.330
What's that?

00:15:13.530 --> 00:15:17.500
A talisman. It's already proven effective against demons like us.

00:15:17.710 --> 00:15:19.540
Isn't that the landlady's letter?

00:15:23.340 --> 00:15:24.840
Footsteps...

00:15:33.890 --> 00:15:38.140
What do you mean by bringing a high school girl here after dark?

00:15:38.350 --> 00:15:39.730
Emi?!

00:15:41.230 --> 00:15:46.900
I see, so you were plotting to get magic from that sealed classroom.

00:15:47.110 --> 00:15:50.570
More like, what are <i>you</i> doing at a school this late?

00:15:50.780 --> 00:15:52.280
Is the hero trespassing?

00:15:52.490 --> 00:15:55.950
U-Um, I'm sorry, but you're not allowed to wear shoes in the building.

00:15:56.160 --> 00:15:59.370
Would you change into these?

00:15:59.580 --> 00:16:04.170
I was tailing you and I saw you sneaking into a school after hours,

00:16:04.380 --> 00:16:05.880
so I came in after you, that's all.

00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:13.680
Anyway, I'm coming with you.
I can't just roll over and let you get more mag--

00:16:15.300 --> 00:16:18.220
Argh, Maou!

00:16:18.430 --> 00:16:21.770
Mr. Maou, is it really okay to leave Miss Yusa behind?

00:16:21.980 --> 00:16:25.110
Totally. She's nothing but trouble.

00:16:25.310 --> 00:16:27.730
Hold right there, Maou!

00:16:27.940 --> 00:16:30.780
--Ugh, what a pain!
--Don't you run from me! I'll kick you!

00:16:30.990 --> 00:16:34.030
Maou! Don't you run from me! I'll kick you!

00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:41.250
What's wrong, Chi?

00:16:41.460 --> 00:16:44.000
I-It's nothing.

00:16:50.010 --> 00:16:52.010
There you are, monster!

00:16:59.560 --> 00:17:00.140
Okay!

00:17:00.350 --> 00:17:01.930
<i>Not</i> okay, you freakin' moron!

00:17:02.140 --> 00:17:06.230
Oh, Miss Yusa, that's called an "anatomical model," and it's just a doll!

00:17:06.440 --> 00:17:07.110
Huh?!

00:17:07.310 --> 00:17:10.360
I'd wager Emilia is the only hero in the whole universe

00:17:10.570 --> 00:17:14.320
to ever chop up an anatomical model with a sacred sword.

00:17:14.530 --> 00:17:16.990
Do normal heroes bust out their sacred swords and attack like that?!

00:17:17.200 --> 00:17:19.490
Do something about this, woman.

00:17:19.700 --> 00:17:22.910
These things've gotta be expensive.
Well, don't come to me for help.

00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:26.580
Th-They'll never know if we don't say anything.

00:17:26.790 --> 00:17:29.130
But of course that's out of the question, right?

00:17:29.340 --> 00:17:33.420
I-It's your fault for sneaking in here to begin with!

00:17:33.630 --> 00:17:36.010
You're a sore loser, Emilia.

00:17:36.220 --> 00:17:38.470
Use your magic to fix it!

00:17:38.680 --> 00:17:43.350
Why should I have to use my precious magic to cover your butt?

00:17:43.560 --> 00:17:46.190
This model only has one heart!

00:17:46.400 --> 00:17:51.150
Mr. Ashiya, I don't know about demons, but humans only ever have one!

00:17:52.650 --> 00:17:55.240
So, the sealed classroom is at the other end of this passageway.

00:17:55.450 --> 00:17:57.240
Look, just keep the sacred sword sheathed.

00:17:57.450 --> 00:17:58.820
Don't take it out until I say.

00:17:59.030 --> 00:18:01.740
I don't take orders from you.

00:18:01.950 --> 00:18:03.950
That's the old schoolhouse there.

00:18:04.160 --> 00:18:09.080
The sealed classroom is on the third floor, all the way up the stairs.

00:18:09.290 --> 00:18:11.170
Okay. Let's go.

00:18:20.180 --> 00:18:22.680
This is the sealed classroom...

00:18:22.890 --> 00:18:26.230
I don't remember it being boarded up, though...

00:18:27.350 --> 00:18:30.520
I told you, put the sword away!

00:18:30.730 --> 00:18:32.610
What is it, Mr. Ashiya?

00:18:32.820 --> 00:18:36.740
There are signs of someone using this door recently.

00:18:40.240 --> 00:18:41.830
They're not attached...

00:18:42.030 --> 00:18:44.830
So this door wasn't sealed after all?

00:18:56.590 --> 00:18:58.800
It feels strangely lived-in.

00:18:59.010 --> 00:19:03.560
It certainly doesn't look like it's been sealed shut for years.

00:19:04.930 --> 00:19:06.270
What's that?

00:19:07.770 --> 00:19:09.310
A game system?

00:19:13.270 --> 00:19:14.730
What now, Urushihara?!

00:19:14.940 --> 00:19:17.360
Are you there yet?

00:19:17.570 --> 00:19:18.990
We just got here.

00:19:19.200 --> 00:19:22.990
What's with you? Quit calling every five seconds! You're startling me!

00:19:23.200 --> 00:19:24.910
Do you see anything on the floor?

00:19:25.120 --> 00:19:27.660
Like, say... a game system?

00:19:27.870 --> 00:19:31.460
Yep, it's here. We have it right now.

00:19:31.670 --> 00:19:34.340
So I was right, that <i>was</i> where it got left.

00:19:34.550 --> 00:19:36.090
--You were "right"?
--Huh?

00:19:36.300 --> 00:19:38.720
Oh, no, nothing!

00:19:38.920 --> 00:19:41.300
Would you mind bringing that home for me?

00:19:41.510 --> 00:19:43.970
Urushihara. Don't tell me you...

00:19:44.180 --> 00:19:45.310
Hmm? What?

00:19:45.510 --> 00:19:48.140
You said this was an easy place for the Gate to open.

00:19:48.350 --> 00:19:51.690
Did you and Olba open the
Gate here to come to Japan?

00:19:51.900 --> 00:19:53.770
Yeah, we did. Didn't I mention that?

00:19:53.980 --> 00:19:55.360
No, you did <i>not</i>!

00:19:55.570 --> 00:19:58.570
So, I lived there with Olba for a while,

00:19:58.780 --> 00:20:02.320
and I accidentally left the game I was playing there...

00:20:02.530 --> 00:20:06.290
Urushihara. You better not have just sent us to bring back your game.

00:20:06.490 --> 00:20:08.500
Of course not!

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:12.540
I thought maybe the Gate opened again and someone else came through, you know?

00:20:12.750 --> 00:20:16.340
So, did you find anything?!
If not, hurry back! I'm hungry!

00:20:16.550 --> 00:20:18.840
U-Um, a pork bowl would be totally fine!

00:20:19.840 --> 00:20:22.380
Who does that Urushihara think he is?!

00:20:22.590 --> 00:20:26.680
Why don't we sell this for cash at BookOn?

00:20:26.890 --> 00:20:28.520
It would supplement our living expenses.

00:20:28.720 --> 00:20:30.850
How miserly are you?

00:20:34.190 --> 00:20:35.650
Udon?

00:20:39.820 --> 00:20:42.700
Dang it, yesterday was a waste of effort!

00:20:52.290 --> 00:20:56.380
Oh, Mr. Maou! I found that on the floor of the science--

00:20:59.670 --> 00:21:03.550
Mr. Maou?! Wake up, Mr. Maou!

00:21:05.890 --> 00:21:08.430
Give that back! It belongs to me!

00:21:08.640 --> 00:21:14.140
Only one hour of gaming per day!
You just be glad it didn't get sold at BookOn!

00:21:25.570 --> 00:21:28.120
Did somebody move in?

00:21:32.960 --> 00:21:34.160
Watch out!

00:21:38.000 --> 00:21:40.590
A-Are you okay?

00:21:40.800 --> 00:21:42.630
Sire! Are you all right?!

00:21:42.840 --> 00:21:47.090
Th-This girl just sort of fell on me all of a sudden...

00:21:47.300 --> 00:21:50.220
Carelessness is... the greatest enemy...

00:21:50.430 --> 00:21:51.930
What?!

00:22:18.170 --> 00:22:23.550
<i>Doko kara asa ni naru? Shizuka na sora</i>

00:22:23.760 --> 00:22:29.090
<i>Minai furi wo shita yubikiri koyubi no saki</i>

00:22:29.300 --> 00:22:39.300
<i>Warawareta tsuki nara kiete</i> <i>yuku n da kinou no houkaku e</i>

00:22:40.110 --> 00:22:45.240
<i>Usotsuki okubyoumono</i> <i>minna matomete boku nara</i>

00:22:45.440 --> 00:22:51.030
<i>Saite ita no wa yume no naka da</i>

00:22:51.240 --> 00:22:56.500
<i>Tsuki no kage ni kakushiteta</i> <i>hontou wa ne naiteta</i>

00:22:56.710 --> 00:23:02.210
<i>Namida wa mou nagarenai karete shimatta no?</i>

00:23:02.420 --> 00:23:08.840
<i>Nani mo ka mo yurusetara</i> <i>nagareru ka mo shirenai kedo</i>

00:23:09.050 --> 00:23:16.390
<i>Mamoritai mono bakari da na</i>
